WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:01:31.174 --> 00:01:32.974
KIM HYE-JIN

3
00:01:40.975 --> 00:01:43.095
TO KIM HYE-JIN

4
00:02:13.508 --> 00:02:14.338
Excuse me!

5
00:02:15.176 --> 00:02:16.336
More beer, please.

6
00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:18.557
Right away! Here's another round.

7
00:02:29.732 --> 00:02:30.822
Here you go!

8
00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:34.364
Here's your beer.

9
00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.701
MY HUSBAND

10
00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:46.076
Yes.

11
00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:47.881
Me? Right now?

12
00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.340
I'm still at Hannam Bridge.

13
00:02:51.462 --> 00:02:53.172
Wow, the night view is spectacular!

14
00:02:53.256 --> 00:02:54.666
Stop lying to me.

15
00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:56.891
You were at the bridge 30 minutes ago.

16
00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.887
Girl, how can you not be here
for my birthday?

17
00:03:00.263 --> 00:03:01.683
I'm almost there.

18
00:03:01.764 --> 00:03:03.224
-We'll order now.
-I'll see you in a bit.

19
00:03:03.641 --> 00:03:05.811
-We're ready to order.
-Okay, I'm coming!

20
00:03:11.482 --> 00:03:13.112
Isn't that girl pretty?

21
00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.913
Here's your cold beer and popcorn.

22
00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:19.196
What's this? Who asked for popcorn?

23
00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.952
Where's our food?

24
00:03:21.326 --> 00:03:22.406
Oh, my!

25
00:03:23.119 --> 00:03:25.869
Our chef must be putting
extra attention into your order

26
00:03:25.955 --> 00:03:27.365
which is why it's taking long.

27
00:03:27.582 --> 00:03:29.582
I'll go and speed things up for you.

28
00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.376
Hold on.

29
00:03:31.961 --> 00:03:34.051
Wasn't that pretty server over there
who took our order

30
00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.670
supposed to wait our table?

31
00:03:35.757 --> 00:03:36.587
Sorry?

32
00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:39.177
-Is this your order?
-Just give us anything.

33
00:03:39.302 --> 00:03:40.142
Understood.

34
00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.428
Oh, right.

35
00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:47.345
I guess I'm the inferior server
when it comes to looks.

36
00:03:47.602 --> 00:03:49.902
I'll tell her to bring you your food,

37
00:03:49.979 --> 00:03:51.689
so don't you worry!

38
00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.747
Are you enjoying the birthday party
I've thrown for you?

39
00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:17.052
I guess.

40
00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.090
Ha-ri.

41
00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.050
Ta-da.

42
00:04:23.388 --> 00:04:24.218
It's my gift to you.

43
00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:27.889
Brand new, directly from Paris--

44
00:04:27.976 --> 00:04:30.846
Here! Wifey! Over here.

45
00:04:31.229 --> 00:04:32.189
Hye-jin!

46
00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:33.522
Here!

47
00:04:37.026 --> 00:04:38.486
Wow, look at that!

48
00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.412
I never thought
you'd have friends like that.

49
00:04:43.074 --> 00:04:43.914
"Like that"?

50
00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:47.374
They say birds of a feather
flock together,

51
00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.503
but her looks and style are ridiculous...

52
00:04:51.874 --> 00:04:54.044
What are you saying, you prick?

53
00:04:55.211 --> 00:04:58.511
-What gives you the right to say that?
-I meant...

54
00:04:59.007 --> 00:05:02.047
Hey, do you even know that friend of mine?

55
00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.640
Do you?

56
00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:07.062
Min Ha-ri, this necklace I got for you...

57
00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:10.177
You can wear it for all I care.

58
00:05:11.936 --> 00:05:14.396
Also, don't ever be
in my line of sight again.

59
00:05:16.691 --> 00:05:18.361
Wifey, come here!

60
00:05:20.069 --> 00:05:20.989
Gosh, I want her.

61
00:05:21.696 --> 00:05:23.696
What took you so long?

62
00:05:23.781 --> 00:05:25.411
I'm sorry!

63
00:05:25.867 --> 00:05:27.077
Here's your present.

64
00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:28.657
What's this?

65
00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:32.456
What's with all the flashing lights?

66
00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.130
I don't think I'm in appropriate attire.

67
00:05:34.208 --> 00:05:35.378
You can dress however you want.

68
00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:37.205
Thanks for coming!

69
00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.420
You haven't eaten yet, have you? Let's go.

70
00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.216
-Come on.
-Wait a second.

71
00:05:42.383 --> 00:05:45.183
The birthday girl should stay.
I can get my own food.

72
00:05:45.261 --> 00:05:46.391
Go and have fun.

73
00:06:08.785 --> 00:06:11.195
STUDENT LOAN INTEREST OF 218,540 WON
DUE ON THE 5TH

74
00:06:28.971 --> 00:06:31.021
Everyone here seems so carefree.

75
00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.820
Well-eaten ghosts look better

76
00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:41.649
and views can't be enjoyed
on an empty stomach.

77
00:06:42.318 --> 00:06:43.608
I've got to eat!

78
00:06:52.703 --> 00:06:53.543
Ha-ri.

79
00:06:53.955 --> 00:06:54.955
Ha-ri!

80
00:06:56.541 --> 00:06:57.381
Ha-ri!

81
00:06:58.292 --> 00:06:59.132
Ha-ri!

82
00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:07.178
Hey, Ha-ri!

83
00:07:07.718 --> 00:07:08.638
Ha-ri!

84
00:07:26.863 --> 00:07:29.413
<i>One day, a thought crossed my mind.</i>

85
00:07:30.032 --> 00:07:36.042
<i>I wondered if lead characters
only exist in movies and dramas.</i>

86
00:07:47.175 --> 00:07:48.545
-Be careful.
-Slow down!

87
00:07:49.218 --> 00:07:51.218
I know how to swim!

88
00:07:51.345 --> 00:07:56.425
<i>Like the popcorn at the bar
that was rejected over hot snacks,</i>

89
00:07:57.143 --> 00:07:59.563
<i>maybe in life too,</i>

90
00:08:00.062 --> 00:08:05.612
<i>people are distinguished as
either a lead or a supporting character.</i>

91
00:08:06.611 --> 00:08:10.451
<i>I'll probably end up as a friend,
three degrees from the lead role.</i>

92
00:08:10.907 --> 00:08:15.537
<i>No, I may simply be an extra
that doesn't even deserve</i>

93
00:08:15.953 --> 00:08:18.663
<i>or can't even shine under the spotlight.</i>

94
00:08:20.374 --> 00:08:22.754
What's that sound? Did she fart?

95
00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.455
Why is she soaking wet?

96
00:09:10.424 --> 00:09:11.474
Did you sleep well?

97
00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:12.887
You're up early.

98
00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:16.888
I'm first!

99
00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.230
Why did you leave
without saying anything last night?

100
00:09:22.353 --> 00:09:25.613
They needed my help at the bar,
so they texted me an SOS.

101
00:09:25.856 --> 00:09:28.226
It's my fault for being good at my job.

102
00:09:28.943 --> 00:09:30.153
Why didn't you pick up your phone?

103
00:09:34.865 --> 00:09:35.865
It drowned.

104
00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:37.450
I need to get it fixed later today.

105
00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:39.754
Did you drop it in the toilet?

106
00:09:41.205 --> 00:09:42.415
How many times is it already?

107
00:09:42.623 --> 00:09:43.833
-You're so clumsy.
-Yes.

108
00:09:43.958 --> 00:09:44.828
Well, that's me.

109
00:09:45.209 --> 00:09:46.089
Anyway, let's eat.

110
00:09:51.841 --> 00:09:54.141
Are you trying to build a tower?

111
00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.640
I have an interview later today.

112
00:09:56.512 --> 00:09:58.312
I'll only be confident on a full stomach.

113
00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:01.144
Haven't you heard back
from your previous interviews?

114
00:10:01.726 --> 00:10:02.766
I haven't.

115
00:10:03.311 --> 00:10:05.901
My only wish is to work late
for someone somewhere,

116
00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:07.320
so why won't they hire me?

117
00:10:07.398 --> 00:10:09.278
I hope every company
that rejected me goes bankrupt!

118
00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:11.236
No, scratch that.

119
00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:14.067
My mom told me to be aware of karma.

120
00:10:14.363 --> 00:10:16.703
Are you done with your speech yet?

121
00:10:19.327 --> 00:10:20.157
JINSUNG MAGAZINE

122
00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:23.870
Oh, no. I'm late!

123
00:10:35.551 --> 00:10:36.681
Which floor are you headed?

124
00:10:37.053 --> 00:10:38.473
-The second.
-Second floor?

125
00:10:39.388 --> 00:10:40.308
Second floor?

126
00:10:40.765 --> 00:10:42.975
-Either of you...
-Aren't you getting off?

127
00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:45.309
One of you should get off.

128
00:10:46.395 --> 00:10:48.435
I thought I got on first.

129
00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:49.861
Didn't I?

130
00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:53.441
I'm going to be late!

131
00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:03.825
You there.

132
00:11:04.955 --> 00:11:05.865
Get in.

133
00:11:27.645 --> 00:11:29.395
JINSUNG MAGAZINE INTERNSHIP INTERVIEW 2015

134
00:11:30.898 --> 00:11:32.688
{\an8}Number 190, Ms. Kim Hye-jin?

135
00:11:32.775 --> 00:11:33.645
Yes.

136
00:11:34.026 --> 00:11:36.026
Where is Youngmin University?

137
00:11:37.363 --> 00:11:38.323
Well...

138
00:11:39.281 --> 00:11:42.491
It's in a nearby area outside of Seoul.

139
00:11:45.162 --> 00:11:47.422
The school isn't well-known,
but it's one with a vision!

140
00:11:47.706 --> 00:11:49.626
The campus is spectacular too.

141
00:11:51.627 --> 00:11:54.547
{\an8}I see you have some work experience.

142
00:11:55.005 --> 00:11:55.835
Yes.

143
00:11:55.965 --> 00:11:59.585
{\an8}But why are all of your past employments
under three months?

144
00:11:59.969 --> 00:12:01.429
One company went bankrupt

145
00:12:01.512 --> 00:12:05.852
{\an8}and the president was arrested
without a warrant in another.

146
00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:13.360
If you let me,
I'll take on the mentality of a worker ant

147
00:12:13.482 --> 00:12:16.652
in order to become a full-time employee
of Jinsung Magazine!

148
00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:22.744
<i>So that's another failed attempt</i>

149
00:12:23.075 --> 00:12:23.945
What's this?

150
00:12:31.333 --> 00:12:32.213
That's cold!

151
00:12:34.086 --> 00:12:36.256
What now? Is it raining?

152
00:12:36.547 --> 00:12:38.047
I hate the rain!

153
00:12:43.345 --> 00:12:44.305
It's go time!

154
00:12:50.561 --> 00:12:52.271
My hair's all frizzy now.

155
00:12:53.314 --> 00:12:54.654
Why did it have to rain?

156
00:13:07.786 --> 00:13:09.366
I'm going to kill her.

157
00:13:15.252 --> 00:13:16.922
You must be so proud of yourself.

158
00:13:17.546 --> 00:13:19.466
Did you seriously just do that in public?

159
00:13:19.548 --> 00:13:20.798
My backbone.

160
00:13:20.966 --> 00:13:22.466
What did I do now?

161
00:13:22.635 --> 00:13:24.295
Who's that guy? Is he your new boyfriend?

162
00:13:24.929 --> 00:13:27.519
No. I'm thinking about
whether I should see him or not.

163
00:13:27.598 --> 00:13:30.848
Why are you kissing him
when you're not even dating?

164
00:13:31.477 --> 00:13:34.477
I'll have to know
if he's a good kisser in order to decide!

165
00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.900
Come on, we're going to the supermarket.

166
00:13:38.359 --> 00:13:39.319
We're out of tissue.

167
00:13:44.823 --> 00:13:48.953
I wish I could borrow your looks
and body for my interviews.

168
00:13:49.453 --> 00:13:52.003
It'd score me additional points.

169
00:13:52.498 --> 00:13:55.208
If I could, I would've lent them
to you a hundred times.

170
00:13:55.918 --> 00:13:59.508
When did you even switch boyfriends again?

171
00:13:59.672 --> 00:14:01.842
Do any of those men
make your heart flutter anyway?

172
00:14:02.424 --> 00:14:03.724
Why does it have to?

173
00:14:03.801 --> 00:14:06.431
If he's nice, I'll give him a shot.

174
00:14:06.637 --> 00:14:08.217
You make it sound so easy.

175
00:14:10.182 --> 00:14:15.272
Then, did you ever find true love
among any of those men?

176
00:14:16.981 --> 00:14:18.151
True love?

177
00:14:19.984 --> 00:14:20.994
What's that?

178
00:14:21.569 --> 00:14:24.279
You miss him when he's not around
and you're happy to be with him.

179
00:14:24.613 --> 00:14:26.033
You do things you'd normally never do

180
00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:28.160
and you see him wherever you go.

181
00:14:28.367 --> 00:14:29.947
Something like that?

182
00:14:31.495 --> 00:14:34.245
True love or whatnot is all just a myth.

183
00:14:39.044 --> 00:14:39.924
Hey!

184
00:14:40.629 --> 00:14:41.799
Mister.

185
00:14:42.131 --> 00:14:43.511
What do you think you're doing?

186
00:14:44.049 --> 00:14:46.839
I was just wondering how much this is.

187
00:14:47.511 --> 00:14:48.801
I won't explain it all,

188
00:14:48.929 --> 00:14:51.059
but it's the same
as squeezing olives for oil.

189
00:14:51.515 --> 00:14:53.805
All men are the same, is what I'm saying.

190
00:14:54.059 --> 00:14:55.769
There's no need to stress about it.

191
00:14:56.061 --> 00:14:57.651
The value of true love?

192
00:14:58.188 --> 00:15:00.978
If it exists, how much would it cost?

193
00:15:01.775 --> 00:15:02.605
What?

194
00:15:02.818 --> 00:15:03.988
That'll be 47,000 won.

195
00:15:05.946 --> 00:15:09.696
Throw out the old-fashioned notions
you have about love

196
00:15:10.784 --> 00:15:12.164
and go on some dates yourself.

197
00:15:13.954 --> 00:15:15.714
Dating is a waste of money.

198
00:15:16.248 --> 00:15:18.208
Besides, no one's even interested in me.

199
00:15:21.795 --> 00:15:23.165
I'll just work on my résumé.

200
00:15:26.759 --> 00:15:29.089
There's so much spam mail.
I don't want a steamy night.

201
00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:33.522
Spam these days looks like real emails.

202
00:15:36.393 --> 00:15:37.273
Wait a minute.

203
00:15:37.853 --> 00:15:38.733
Ji Sung-joon?

204
00:15:38.812 --> 00:15:39.982
HYE-JIN, IT'S ME, SUNG-JOON

205
00:15:40.064 --> 00:15:41.114
Ji Sung-joon would be...

206
00:15:42.316 --> 00:15:43.646
Can it be that Ji Sung-joon?

207
00:15:49.156 --> 00:15:50.486
IT'S BEEN A WHILE,
DO YOU REMEMBER ME?

208
00:15:50.574 --> 00:15:51.994
{\an8}I'LL BE BACK IN KOREA SOON.
IF YOU HAVE TIME, LET'S MEET UP.

209
00:15:53.369 --> 00:15:54.949
Is it really him?

210
00:15:55.162 --> 00:15:56.042
What is it?

211
00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:57.410
Who's Ji Sung-joon?

212
00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:00.331
Don't you remember?

213
00:16:00.584 --> 00:16:03.004
When your father relocated
to the office in Japan,

214
00:16:03.087 --> 00:16:04.457
a family moved into your old house.

215
00:16:05.589 --> 00:16:06.719
That's right.

216
00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.090
That fat kid?

217
00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:11.050
Stop right there, fat boy!

218
00:16:13.347 --> 00:16:15.347
What are you doing in my house?

219
00:16:16.684 --> 00:16:17.814
No, I...

220
00:16:19.853 --> 00:16:20.813
Dad!

221
00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:23.900
Who's that fatty?

222
00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:25.650
What a loser.

223
00:16:27.653 --> 00:16:28.863
Is he the neighborhood idiot?

224
00:16:29.238 --> 00:16:32.448
When I saw him at the house,
I thought he was just some loser.

225
00:16:33.534 --> 00:16:35.334
I was so surprised when I heard

226
00:16:35.411 --> 00:16:37.121
that the two of you
had become best friends.

227
00:16:38.747 --> 00:16:41.077
But why is the fatty contacting you now?

228
00:16:43.127 --> 00:16:44.087
He wants to meet.

229
00:16:44.461 --> 00:16:45.341
What?

230
00:17:00.686 --> 00:17:03.976
So that naive Sung-joon is coming back.

231
00:17:18.328 --> 00:17:19.198
It's go time!

232
00:17:24.501 --> 00:17:25.591
Wifey!

233
00:17:28.047 --> 00:17:31.047
Is today the day you're meeting Fatty?

234
00:17:32.176 --> 00:17:33.586
Have you talked to him on the phone?

235
00:17:33.677 --> 00:17:34.927
No, it was just emails.

236
00:17:35.012 --> 00:17:36.602
I'll call him when I get there.

237
00:17:37.139 --> 00:17:39.599
Hey, do you think there's
a pay phone there?

238
00:17:40.225 --> 00:17:41.225
A pay phone?

239
00:17:41.435 --> 00:17:43.095
Right, your phone's getting fixed.

240
00:17:43.437 --> 00:17:44.977
Just take my phone instead.

241
00:17:45.481 --> 00:17:47.111
Won't it be inconvenient for you?

242
00:17:47.441 --> 00:17:50.691
It's fine. I'm tired of all of these guys
calling me anyway.

243
00:17:50.778 --> 00:17:54.108
I want to smack you
but I can't because it's true.

244
00:17:55.783 --> 00:17:57.453
Why are you meeting that fatty anyway?

245
00:17:57.826 --> 00:17:59.786
I doubt it'll benefit you in any way.

246
00:18:00.496 --> 00:18:02.406
We were really close friends.

247
00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:04.540
And he was kind of...

248
00:18:06.752 --> 00:18:08.052
my first love.

249
00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:09.710
No way.

250
00:18:10.214 --> 00:18:12.054
I didn't know
that your standards were so low.

251
00:18:12.508 --> 00:18:14.638
They're practically buried underground.

252
00:18:14.843 --> 00:18:16.723
Fine. Keep making fun of me.

253
00:18:17.888 --> 00:18:21.888
You can say whatever you like,
but he and I share a special relationship.

254
00:18:23.018 --> 00:18:24.388
I wonder how he's changed!

255
00:18:24.561 --> 00:18:26.441
Stop it, you'll cause us to crash.

256
00:19:38.302 --> 00:19:39.262
All right.

257
00:19:44.183 --> 00:19:46.023
-Why?
-Come here.

258
00:19:50.147 --> 00:19:52.107
-What are you doing?
-Hold still.

259
00:19:52.191 --> 00:19:53.571
You're meeting with your first love.

260
00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:57.650
There, much better.

261
00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:02.580
This work is Renoir's
<i>Dance in the Country</i>.

262
00:20:02.784 --> 00:20:04.834
In the painting, the main character

263
00:20:04.912 --> 00:20:07.002
is Renoir's friend Paul
and his wife-to-be.

264
00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:09.290
It might not actually be those two.

265
00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:16.670
I mean, based on the perspective,
the lead can always change.

266
00:20:20.886 --> 00:20:23.216
I didn't mean to interrupt your class.
I'm sorry.

267
00:20:40.614 --> 00:20:42.494
How do you do? I'm Kim Shin-hyuk,

268
00:20:42.658 --> 00:20:46.158
<i>The Most Korea</i>'s handsome features editor
assigned to cover this exhibit.

269
00:20:48.121 --> 00:20:49.371
<i>Sung-joon, it's Hye-jin.</i>

270
00:20:49.665 --> 00:20:50.665
<i>I've arrived.</i>

271
00:20:50.749 --> 00:20:52.209
<i>Call me at this number when you get here.</i>

272
00:21:07.057 --> 00:21:08.637
Just five minutes left!

273
00:21:24.616 --> 00:21:26.576
Sung-joon. It's you, right?

274
00:21:28.287 --> 00:21:30.577
It's been so long!

275
00:21:31.665 --> 00:21:34.535
You haven't changed at all!

276
00:21:34.835 --> 00:21:35.665
Who are you?

277
00:21:39.047 --> 00:21:42.297
Are you not Sung-joon?

278
00:21:42.884 --> 00:21:43.724
Sir?

279
00:21:45.387 --> 00:21:46.557
No, I'm not!

280
00:21:47.431 --> 00:21:49.771
I'm so sorry. I apologize.

281
00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:51.560
Ma'am, what's with the violence?

282
00:21:51.727 --> 00:21:53.307
I'm not old enough to be called ma'am.

283
00:21:55.689 --> 00:21:56.609
Of course you are.

284
00:21:59.234 --> 00:22:00.154
Hold on.

285
00:22:03.113 --> 00:22:03.953
Hello?

286
00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:05.740
<i>Hye-jin, this is Sung-joon.</i>

287
00:22:06.366 --> 00:22:07.736
Yes, Sung-joon.

288
00:22:08.243 --> 00:22:09.293
<i>Where are you now?</i>

289
00:22:09.953 --> 00:22:11.043
I'm near the fountain.

290
00:22:11.288 --> 00:22:12.158
The fountain?

291
00:22:13.081 --> 00:22:14.831
I'm near the fountain too.

292
00:22:19.963 --> 00:22:21.133
I think I've found you.

293
00:22:21.423 --> 00:22:22.263
Really?

294
00:22:22.674 --> 00:22:25.054
I don't see you anywhere.

295
00:22:25.927 --> 00:22:26.757
Don't you see me?

296
00:22:27.763 --> 00:22:28.603
Here.

297
00:22:36.271 --> 00:22:37.401
No way.

298
00:22:49.659 --> 00:22:50.539
Hye-jin.

299
00:22:50.744 --> 00:22:51.584
Hold on a second.

300
00:22:54.873 --> 00:22:57.083
<i>In the confusion of trying
to make ends meet all the time,</i>

301
00:22:57.167 --> 00:22:58.667
<i>I had forgotten one important fact!</i>

302
00:22:58.877 --> 00:23:01.957
<i>The image he has of me
in the past was at least like this.</i>

303
00:23:02.172 --> 00:23:05.382
Sit down next to the friend
you want to get to know.

304
00:23:10.055 --> 00:23:11.135
<i>Like this.</i>

305
00:23:11.348 --> 00:23:12.268
First prize goes to

306
00:23:12.516 --> 00:23:14.596
Kim Hye-jin from fifth grade.

307
00:23:14.684 --> 00:23:18.984
-Kim Hye-jin!
-Kim Hye-jin!

308
00:23:19.064 --> 00:23:21.024
<i>Or something like this.</i>

309
00:23:21.733 --> 00:23:24.953
-Fatty, fat boy!
-Look at this loser.

310
00:23:25.153 --> 00:23:27.323
Hey, stop making fun of Sung-joon!

311
00:23:29.699 --> 00:23:32.369
<i>This is the very least
he would expect from me!</i>

312
00:23:35.163 --> 00:23:36.163
Are you Hye-jin?

313
00:23:37.249 --> 00:23:38.129
No, I'm not.

314
00:23:38.708 --> 00:23:39.578
I'm so sorry.

315
00:23:39.876 --> 00:23:40.746
Honey.

316
00:23:41.002 --> 00:23:42.052
Hye-jin, where are you?

317
00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:00.520
Wasn't that pretty server
over there who took our order

318
00:24:00.730 --> 00:24:02.020
supposed to wait our table?

319
00:24:02.107 --> 00:24:04.277
Where is Youngmin University?

320
00:24:04.609 --> 00:24:08.359
<i>Applicant Kim Hye-jin has been rejected.</i>

321
00:24:08.613 --> 00:24:10.323
<i>-Rejected.
-Rejection.</i>

322
00:24:10.407 --> 00:24:12.367
<i>You've been rejected.</i>

323
00:24:14.119 --> 00:24:15.869
<i>We used to be wealthy,</i>

324
00:24:16.204 --> 00:24:19.334
<i>but my father's business went bankrupt
after Sung-joon moved away.</i>

325
00:24:20.458 --> 00:24:23.748
<i>I used to be pretty like my mom,</i>

326
00:24:24.379 --> 00:24:28.629
<i>but my dad's traits
that weren't as appealing</i>

327
00:24:28.967 --> 00:24:34.257
<i>began to show in late adolescence.</i>

328
00:24:34.639 --> 00:24:38.349
<i>Before I knew it,
I had already turned out like this.</i>

329
00:24:46.193 --> 00:24:47.863
Hey, Kim Hye-jin.

330
00:24:49.321 --> 00:24:51.661
Why are you back already?
Didn't you meet Fatty?

331
00:24:53.074 --> 00:24:53.914
About that...

332
00:24:59.164 --> 00:25:03.044
Let's just go home, Ha-ri.

333
00:25:06.463 --> 00:25:09.593
If he ended up turning into a hot guy,
you should definitely go after him.

334
00:25:10.300 --> 00:25:11.260
Why would you run away?

335
00:25:11.468 --> 00:25:14.258
He didn't even imagine
that I'd turn out like this.

336
00:25:14.763 --> 00:25:16.813
I was right in front of him,
but he didn't recognize me.

337
00:25:17.349 --> 00:25:21.189
There's no more trace
of the pretty girl that he used to know.

338
00:25:22.437 --> 00:25:25.437
I knew that meeting him
would be more humiliating

339
00:25:25.982 --> 00:25:27.402
<i>and that scared me.</i>

340
00:25:27.692 --> 00:25:29.112
<i>It's why I ran away.</i>

341
00:25:29.861 --> 00:25:32.661
I was eager to see him again,

342
00:25:37.077 --> 00:25:38.247
but I was too naive.

343
00:25:39.871 --> 00:25:42.711
Don't say that.
There's nothing wrong with you.

344
00:25:42.832 --> 00:25:44.542
You're a good catch!

345
00:25:44.709 --> 00:25:45.629
Just meet him.

346
00:25:45.710 --> 00:25:46.880
If he asks me what I do,

347
00:25:47.587 --> 00:25:49.207
do I tell him I'm unemployed at 30?

348
00:25:49.547 --> 00:25:51.047
If he says he couldn't recognize me,

349
00:25:51.591 --> 00:25:53.131
do I apologize for looking ugly?

350
00:25:53.510 --> 00:25:54.470
Hey.

351
00:25:54.552 --> 00:25:58.182
I want to preserve the memories
of his first love.

352
00:25:59.307 --> 00:26:00.767
If I don't meet him,

353
00:26:01.142 --> 00:26:05.022
he'll keep those great memories of me.

354
00:26:05.563 --> 00:26:06.733
Kim Hye-jin.

355
00:26:08.441 --> 00:26:09.901
You're being ridiculous.

356
00:26:10.610 --> 00:26:12.360
Stop talking like an idiot

357
00:26:12.696 --> 00:26:14.156
and meet him right away.

358
00:26:14.489 --> 00:26:16.449
Being a decent guy,
he'll say he's happy to see me,

359
00:26:16.908 --> 00:26:18.578
but I bet he'll be flustered.

360
00:26:19.035 --> 00:26:20.745
"She's gone.

361
00:26:21.121 --> 00:26:23.581
The girl that I once loved is gone."

362
00:26:23.957 --> 00:26:24.917
That's what he'll think.

363
00:26:26.126 --> 00:26:27.036
Oh, please.

364
00:26:27.210 --> 00:26:31.970
If only I could borrow
your looks and body for today.

365
00:26:33.341 --> 00:26:34.381
Wait, Ha-ri.

366
00:26:35.176 --> 00:26:37.296
I've just thought of something...

367
00:26:38.930 --> 00:26:41.350
and I think you can help me.

368
00:26:57.032 --> 00:26:58.412
Sung-joon.

369
00:27:05.248 --> 00:27:07.288
Kim Hye-jin?

370
00:27:09.169 --> 00:27:10.209
You must be Hye-jin.

371
00:27:11.004 --> 00:27:12.844
Sorry, I'm late.

372
00:27:15.008 --> 00:27:16.088
It's been a while.

373
00:27:17.010 --> 00:27:17.930
Have you been well?

374
00:27:23.183 --> 00:27:24.023
Hye-jin.

375
00:27:59.302 --> 00:28:02.312
I've missed you, Kim Hye-jin.

376
00:28:08.686 --> 00:28:09.686
Hey, kid!

377
00:28:11.022 --> 00:28:11.862
Did you move here?

378
00:28:12.315 --> 00:28:15.355
My best friend Ha-ri used to live there.

379
00:28:16.194 --> 00:28:18.574
I'm in the fifth grade, what about you?

380
00:28:18.947 --> 00:28:20.777
Third grade, fourth grade?

381
00:28:27.205 --> 00:28:28.955
Hey, kid!

382
00:28:32.252 --> 00:28:33.592
Let's welcome our new student.

383
00:28:33.670 --> 00:28:35.710
His name is Ji Sung-joon
and he just transferred here.

384
00:28:36.256 --> 00:28:38.296
Hey, you're not a kid!

385
00:28:38.383 --> 00:28:39.553
She called him a kid!

386
00:28:41.052 --> 00:28:43.302
That's not a kid. It's a fatty!

387
00:28:56.234 --> 00:28:57.904
My mom asked me to give this to you.

388
00:28:58.486 --> 00:29:02.486
Also, I'm sorry. You're shorter,
so I thought you were younger than me.

389
00:29:02.949 --> 00:29:04.659
You should've told me that you weren't.

390
00:29:08.747 --> 00:29:09.907
Are you working on a puzzle?

391
00:29:11.499 --> 00:29:13.079
I saw that painting in a textbook!

392
00:29:14.502 --> 00:29:16.882
I never realized there was a person
in the corner before.

393
00:29:18.298 --> 00:29:19.258
You found her.

394
00:29:20.383 --> 00:29:22.303
That girl is hiding.

395
00:29:23.803 --> 00:29:24.803
Hiding?

396
00:29:25.346 --> 00:29:27.426
She really does look like she's hiding.

397
00:29:28.349 --> 00:29:29.479
I wonder what she's looking at.

398
00:29:30.226 --> 00:29:32.686
Does she want to dance on stage too?

399
00:29:33.646 --> 00:29:38.066
In my opinion, she's watching the man

400
00:29:38.526 --> 00:29:40.196
because she secretly likes him.

401
00:29:40.779 --> 00:29:42.449
That could be true too.

402
00:29:42.989 --> 00:29:45.449
It's like finding her
in a hidden picture puzzle.

403
00:29:46.451 --> 00:29:48.291
A hidden picture puzzle?

404
00:29:49.287 --> 00:29:52.247
Look. You can't see her
unless you look closely.

405
00:29:52.415 --> 00:29:53.705
Just like a hidden picture puzzle.

406
00:29:54.793 --> 00:29:55.633
You're right.

407
00:29:55.794 --> 00:29:57.844
It really is like a hidden picture puzzle.

408
00:30:00.256 --> 00:30:02.126
<i>I didn't want to disappoint my first love.</i>

409
00:30:03.843 --> 00:30:08.563
<i>In front of him, I could see myself
being the popcorn everyone discards.</i>

410
00:30:10.517 --> 00:30:13.807
<i>So in the end, on that very day,</i>

411
00:30:14.979 --> 00:30:20.739
<i>I watched him from afar
as I hid in the background.</i>

412
00:30:24.364 --> 00:30:26.324
<i>Don't make any mistakes
and do as we planned.</i>

413
00:30:29.452 --> 00:30:30.752
Here is our menu.

414
00:30:34.541 --> 00:30:35.751
Should we go ahead and order?

415
00:30:36.459 --> 00:30:37.289
Sure.

416
00:30:43.216 --> 00:30:44.926
Miss, would you like to place an order?

417
00:30:47.011 --> 00:30:47.851
Miss?

418
00:30:48.888 --> 00:30:49.718
Miss.

419
00:30:50.682 --> 00:30:51.522
What?

420
00:30:52.684 --> 00:30:53.894
Would you like to order?

421
00:30:57.146 --> 00:30:58.056
Give me this, this one.

422
00:30:58.189 --> 00:31:00.899
The grilled shrimp and caviar
with the filet mignon steak.

423
00:31:00.984 --> 00:31:01.944
Coming right up.

424
00:31:02.026 --> 00:31:02.856
Sure.

425
00:31:02.944 --> 00:31:03.784
What?

426
00:31:03.862 --> 00:31:04.782
No!

427
00:31:05.405 --> 00:31:08.865
Forget the filet mignon steak
and give me a cup of coffee.

428
00:31:09.158 --> 00:31:11.408
-Coffee.
-Sure thing.

429
00:31:15.707 --> 00:31:17.417
I don't know what to ask you first.

430
00:31:18.209 --> 00:31:19.669
I have so many questions.

431
00:31:22.505 --> 00:31:23.375
What about work?

432
00:31:23.965 --> 00:31:25.005
What kind of work do you do?

433
00:31:25.425 --> 00:31:27.545
When he asks you what you do,
tell him this.

434
00:31:28.011 --> 00:31:29.301
I'm still studying.

435
00:31:29.679 --> 00:31:32.679
It's been somewhat of a calling.

436
00:31:33.391 --> 00:31:34.891
So you're still in school.

437
00:31:35.351 --> 00:31:36.191
What about you?

438
00:31:36.436 --> 00:31:40.056
I'm involved in art directing.

439
00:31:40.857 --> 00:31:42.857
<i>I have no idea what that is.</i>

440
00:31:42.984 --> 00:31:44.784
Oh, I see.

441
00:31:45.737 --> 00:31:47.317
Are your parents doing well?

442
00:31:47.655 --> 00:31:48.525
Of course.

443
00:31:48.615 --> 00:31:49.695
My mom and dad are doing...

444
00:31:50.450 --> 00:31:51.330
Well!

445
00:31:55.204 --> 00:31:58.754
They're both doing well.

446
00:32:01.544 --> 00:32:02.424
Are you okay?

447
00:32:11.429 --> 00:32:13.639
How about your parents?

448
00:32:14.641 --> 00:32:18.271
My father is in Seattle
and I was in New York for work.

449
00:32:18.937 --> 00:32:22.397
I don't see him often,
but he's doing well as always.

450
00:32:23.024 --> 00:32:23.904
What about your mother?

451
00:32:27.987 --> 00:32:28.817
What?

452
00:32:33.993 --> 00:32:34.873
His mother passed away.

453
00:32:40.291 --> 00:32:41.831
Oh, gosh.

454
00:32:43.586 --> 00:32:45.086
Your father...

455
00:32:45.797 --> 00:32:49.127
I thought he might've remarried.

456
00:32:51.052 --> 00:32:51.932
I see.

457
00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:54.720
Yes, he did remarry.

458
00:32:55.098 --> 00:32:56.428
It's been about seven years now.

459
00:32:56.808 --> 00:32:59.348
I had a feeling that he did,
which is why I asked.

460
00:33:01.980 --> 00:33:05.780
But why did you decide
to contact me all of a sudden?

461
00:33:08.653 --> 00:33:11.283
I was cleaning up my place
before I came back to Korea

462
00:33:11.739 --> 00:33:13.069
and I found a box.

463
00:33:13.741 --> 00:33:15.331
I didn't know I still had them

464
00:33:16.077 --> 00:33:18.617
and I found the letters
that you used to write me.

465
00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:22.290
Reading them reminded me of our childhood

466
00:33:23.167 --> 00:33:26.127
and I suddenly missed you like crazy.

467
00:33:26.754 --> 00:33:27.714
I see.

468
00:33:28.673 --> 00:33:31.383
Why did you stop contacting me back then?

469
00:33:31.926 --> 00:33:35.046
If he asks why I stopped
contacting him, tell him this.

470
00:33:35.555 --> 00:33:40.015
After you left the country,
we also left to live in Japan.

471
00:33:40.643 --> 00:33:43.023
I lost your address during the move.

472
00:33:44.063 --> 00:33:45.943
I've been wondering about you too though.

473
00:33:47.150 --> 00:33:49.070
It's nice to finally meet you again.

474
00:33:49.986 --> 00:33:51.606
And so the mystery is solved.

475
00:33:52.822 --> 00:33:55.582
My letters kept coming back,
so I wondered what happened.

476
00:33:56.743 --> 00:33:57.703
I see.

477
00:33:58.327 --> 00:34:01.117
Do you remember the puzzle back then?
It was in the box too.

478
00:34:01.748 --> 00:34:04.208
Puzzle?

479
00:34:05.626 --> 00:34:07.336
Oh, the puzzle.

480
00:34:09.130 --> 00:34:10.210
Right.

481
00:34:16.596 --> 00:34:17.596
THE HIDDEN GIRL

482
00:34:18.681 --> 00:34:19.771
Are you all right?

483
00:34:20.099 --> 00:34:21.349
{\an8}THE HIDDEN GIRL

484
00:34:21.434 --> 00:34:23.814
{\an8}Oh, the hidden girl!

485
00:34:26.397 --> 00:34:27.607
You remember?

486
00:34:30.693 --> 00:34:33.033
I had forgotten that I had it

487
00:34:33.738 --> 00:34:37.528
but then remembered
that we used to put it together.

488
00:34:38.826 --> 00:34:40.116
I suddenly felt grateful.

489
00:34:42.455 --> 00:34:46.785
Until I met you, I was always alone,

490
00:34:47.919 --> 00:34:50.629
but I realized something
when you became my friend.

491
00:34:52.757 --> 00:34:56.887
Even if you have
only one friend in the entire world,

492
00:34:58.262 --> 00:34:59.852
you won't be lonely

493
00:35:00.890 --> 00:35:02.520
and that life could be fun.

494
00:35:04.227 --> 00:35:08.767
And I was glad
that the one friend I had...

495
00:35:11.025 --> 00:35:15.195
was such a great person,
which you truly were.

496
00:35:17.865 --> 00:35:22.995
Reminiscing made me be grateful,
and I started to miss you.

497
00:35:24.789 --> 00:35:26.039
It's why I wanted to see you.

498
00:35:30.545 --> 00:35:31.745
Now that I'm here,

499
00:35:33.047 --> 00:35:34.467
I think I've made the right choice.

500
00:35:46.269 --> 00:35:50.769
I think I've made the right choice too
by hiding.

501
00:35:57.613 --> 00:35:59.073
I'll drop you off where you live.

502
00:35:59.740 --> 00:36:01.330
It's okay. I drove here too.

503
00:36:02.326 --> 00:36:03.326
Really?

504
00:36:04.787 --> 00:36:08.707
Then I guess we'll part ways for today.

505
00:36:09.083 --> 00:36:09.963
Sung-joon.

506
00:36:11.043 --> 00:36:12.503
I have something to tell you.

507
00:36:13.337 --> 00:36:15.127
To preserve our precious memories

508
00:36:15.214 --> 00:36:18.594
and bring this night to a beautiful end,

509
00:36:19.302 --> 00:36:20.512
tell him this.

510
00:36:20.928 --> 00:36:23.428
I'm going overseas to study.

511
00:36:24.473 --> 00:36:25.393
What?

512
00:36:25.600 --> 00:36:28.310
I regret having to tell you this
on our reunion,

513
00:36:28.811 --> 00:36:30.521
but I've been planning it for some time.

514
00:36:33.232 --> 00:36:36.612
Oh, so that's what you had planned.

515
00:36:37.904 --> 00:36:38.864
Where are you headed?

516
00:36:40.448 --> 00:36:41.278
What?

517
00:36:42.950 --> 00:36:44.120
GREAT BRITAIN'S MAGICIAN OF LIGHT

518
00:36:45.203 --> 00:36:46.163
To England.

519
00:36:47.371 --> 00:36:48.211
I'm going to England.

520
00:36:50.291 --> 00:36:51.421
When are you leaving?

521
00:36:52.293 --> 00:36:53.713
-Tomorrow.
-Tomorrow?

522
00:36:53.961 --> 00:36:55.171
Yes, tomorrow.

523
00:36:55.421 --> 00:36:56.301
Tomorrow?

524
00:36:56.505 --> 00:36:57.335
Yes.

525
00:37:02.178 --> 00:37:04.558
What am I going to do now?

526
00:37:06.557 --> 00:37:08.557
It feels too early to part ways like this.

527
00:37:10.186 --> 00:37:11.476
We'll contact each other again.

528
00:37:12.521 --> 00:37:13.361
Sure.

529
00:37:14.732 --> 00:37:18.362
I go to London
a couple of times a year for work,

530
00:37:18.903 --> 00:37:20.823
so I guess I'll see you then.

531
00:37:21.572 --> 00:37:22.532
Good luck in England

532
00:37:24.700 --> 00:37:26.410
and keep in touch.

533
00:37:27.620 --> 00:37:29.790
Sure. It was nice to see you today.

534
00:37:30.957 --> 00:37:33.417
I'll be leaving now.

535
00:37:37.046 --> 00:37:38.256
Wait, Hye-jin.

536
00:37:42.802 --> 00:37:43.642
Yes?

537
00:37:44.387 --> 00:37:46.177
Can you wait here for just five minutes?

538
00:37:46.722 --> 00:37:48.432
-Five minutes?
-Yes, exactly five minutes.

539
00:37:48.891 --> 00:37:49.771
I'll be back before then.

540
00:37:50.685 --> 00:37:52.685
Wait, where are you going?

541
00:38:03.030 --> 00:38:03.860
Welcome.

542
00:38:03.948 --> 00:38:04.868
Yes, hello.

543
00:38:09.787 --> 00:38:12.327
AUGUSTE RENOIR

544
00:38:15.835 --> 00:38:16.665
I made it back in time.

545
00:38:17.169 --> 00:38:18.169
Where did you go?

546
00:38:24.385 --> 00:38:26.175
I wanted to get you a parting gift.

547
00:38:26.971 --> 00:38:28.351
It'll be useful in London.

548
00:38:28.931 --> 00:38:30.471
Use this to avoid the thing you hate.

549
00:38:31.350 --> 00:38:32.180
Right.

550
00:38:33.269 --> 00:38:34.099
Thanks.

551
00:38:39.358 --> 00:38:42.358
Good luck and keep in touch.

552
00:38:44.739 --> 00:38:46.869
Yes, it was nice to see you again.

553
00:38:47.491 --> 00:38:48.331
Goodbye.

554
00:39:02.798 --> 00:39:03.758
Have a good trip.

555
00:39:27.281 --> 00:39:29.331
How can a person change so much?

556
00:39:30.534 --> 00:39:33.754
Only a transforming robot
could make such a drastic change.

557
00:39:35.873 --> 00:39:37.173
He gave you this gift.

558
00:39:38.125 --> 00:39:40.125
He mentioned something
about avoiding what you hate.

559
00:39:40.419 --> 00:39:41.459
Something I hate?

560
00:39:49.720 --> 00:39:51.640
It's only an umbrella.

561
00:39:52.348 --> 00:39:53.808
I thought it was something special.

562
00:39:54.558 --> 00:39:55.638
I'm out of beer.

563
00:39:56.394 --> 00:39:58.484
Stay here, I'll get one for you.

564
00:39:59.980 --> 00:40:01.150
That's a first.

565
00:40:13.702 --> 00:40:15.452
Wait, are you asleep?

566
00:40:17.123 --> 00:40:19.963
At least wash off your makeup
before you sleep.

567
00:40:20.876 --> 00:40:21.706
Ha-ri.

568
00:40:22.253 --> 00:40:23.093
Min Ha-ri!

569
00:40:26.257 --> 00:40:28.757
You must be so tired from all the acting.

570
00:40:38.018 --> 00:40:41.768
I'm sorry I'm such an ugly friend.

571
00:41:26.108 --> 00:41:28.148
{\an8}JI SUNG-JOON: I MISS YOU, HYE-JIN!

572
00:41:28.235 --> 00:41:30.025
{\an8}JI SUNG-JOON: I GOT YOUR LETTER.

573
00:41:34.033 --> 00:41:35.243
{\an8}JI SUNG-JOON: WHEN SHOULD WE MEET?

574
00:41:35.326 --> 00:41:36.286
DELETE ALL CHECKED ITEMS?

575
00:41:42.374 --> 00:41:45.214
-What are you talking about?
-That's not it!

576
00:41:45.336 --> 00:41:49.836
-I'll hold the best birthday party!
-Count me in!

577
00:41:58.641 --> 00:42:00.481
Hey, it's dangerous. Sit down, kid!

578
00:42:00.893 --> 00:42:03.443
The door! Mister, open this door!

579
00:42:03.646 --> 00:42:06.436
Please open this door! Mister, please!

580
00:42:06.857 --> 00:42:08.187
Open this door!

581
00:42:08.275 --> 00:42:10.435
Mister, open this door.

582
00:42:11.445 --> 00:42:14.865
Please! Mister, open this door.

583
00:42:15.115 --> 00:42:17.075
Mister, open this door for me!

584
00:42:17.159 --> 00:42:17.989
Open the door.

585
00:42:33.551 --> 00:42:34.471
Mom.

586
00:42:35.052 --> 00:42:35.892
Mom.

587
00:42:36.262 --> 00:42:37.722
I'm afraid.

588
00:42:38.305 --> 00:42:39.265
Mom.

589
00:42:40.307 --> 00:42:41.517
I'm afraid of the rain.

590
00:42:41.892 --> 00:42:44.982
Mom, I'm afraid of the rain!

591
00:42:48.524 --> 00:42:50.364
Sung-joon, what's wrong?

592
00:42:50.734 --> 00:42:52.614
-Are you okay?
-Mom, the rain.

593
00:42:52.695 --> 00:42:55.405
I'm afraid of the rain.

594
00:42:56.740 --> 00:42:57.580
Let's go.

595
00:42:59.368 --> 00:43:00.448
I'm afraid of the rain.

596
00:43:04.373 --> 00:43:05.543
Mom, the rain.

597
00:43:05.708 --> 00:43:06.628
My mom, she...

598
00:43:07.459 --> 00:43:10.549
I'm afraid of the rain!

599
00:43:34.194 --> 00:43:36.784
I'm here with you now.

600
00:43:38.741 --> 00:43:41.791
I'll be your umbrella.

601
00:44:12.024 --> 00:44:14.034
You hold onto the hidden girl.

602
00:44:14.610 --> 00:44:17.910
A puzzle isn't complete
without all of the pieces.

603
00:44:18.489 --> 00:44:21.619
We'll meet again someday
and complete the puzzle.

604
00:44:23.827 --> 00:44:24.787
Okay.

605
00:44:26.705 --> 00:44:27.665
Bye, Sung-joon.

606
00:45:10.499 --> 00:45:12.419
DELETE ALL CHECKED ITEMS?

607
00:45:18.465 --> 00:45:19.875
DELETE ALL CHECKED ITEMS?

608
00:45:22.052 --> 00:45:23.052
ALL ITEMS HAVE BEEN DELETED

609
00:45:25.514 --> 00:45:28.484
<i>Goodbye, my first love.</i>

610
00:45:34.606 --> 00:45:35.436
What's the matter?

611
00:45:36.817 --> 00:45:38.277
What? Why?

612
00:45:38.360 --> 00:45:44.660
<i>Sometimes, without any warning,
your life takes an unexpected turn.</i>

613
00:45:45.075 --> 00:45:48.245
Ha-ri, what am I going to do?

614
00:45:48.537 --> 00:45:53.957
-Why, what's the matter?
-<i>Sometimes, you never get your way.</i>

615
00:45:54.168 --> 00:45:55.628
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR INTERNSHIP
AT JINSUNG MAGAZINE

616
00:45:57.254 --> 00:46:02.594
<i>And other times, things work out fine.</i>

617
00:46:04.553 --> 00:46:05.893
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

618
00:46:05.971 --> 00:46:07.011
Congratulations, Kim Hye-jin!

619
00:46:14.563 --> 00:46:15.403
Min Ha-ri!

620
00:46:36.585 --> 00:46:38.415
I did it!

621
00:46:40.255 --> 00:46:45.635
-Employee!
-Employee!

622
00:46:51.767 --> 00:46:53.477
{\an8}EMPLOYEE

623
00:47:10.702 --> 00:47:13.082
<i>Kim Hye-jin, it's been a long road.</i>

624
00:47:13.413 --> 00:47:15.923
<i>I have a feeling
that good things are in store.</i>

625
00:47:32.724 --> 00:47:34.694
<i>Things may not always go my way,</i>

626
00:47:34.768 --> 00:47:36.848
<i>but it'll only help me grow stronger.</i>

627
00:47:37.104 --> 00:47:38.444
<i>It's time to forget about the past</i>

628
00:47:38.605 --> 00:47:42.355
<i>and start a brand new chapter
in Kim Hye-jin's life!</i>

629
00:47:42.609 --> 00:47:43.609
Onward!

630
00:47:46.113 --> 00:47:47.533
Onward I go!

631
00:47:54.955 --> 00:47:56.285
What a waste.

632
00:48:11.680 --> 00:48:13.560
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

633
00:48:19.271 --> 00:48:21.441
If you're really injured,
I'll help you up.

634
00:48:22.107 --> 00:48:23.357
But if you're embarrassed,

635
00:48:23.775 --> 00:48:25.985
I advise that you get up
and make a run for it.

636
00:48:35.579 --> 00:48:37.829
Do you want to try and get up?

637
00:48:40.584 --> 00:48:42.004
No.

638
00:48:43.712 --> 00:48:44.882
My front tooth.

639
00:48:46.340 --> 00:48:49.050
I think I've lost my front tooth!

640
00:48:50.010 --> 00:48:51.010
My tooth!

641
00:48:51.595 --> 00:48:52.965
My tooth!

642
00:48:53.263 --> 00:48:54.143
This?

643
00:48:56.391 --> 00:48:57.271
This is just chewing gum.

644
00:49:00.937 --> 00:49:01.767
What?

645
00:49:07.653 --> 00:49:08.493
They're all there.

646
00:49:09.112 --> 00:49:09.992
Why don't you get up?

647
00:49:10.238 --> 00:49:11.318
I'm going to be late!

648
00:49:15.577 --> 00:49:16.867
What a weird woman.

649
00:49:22.125 --> 00:49:23.875
Black loafers with white socks?

650
00:49:26.380 --> 00:49:27.880
MANAGEMENT SUPPORT DEPARTMENT

651
00:49:30.258 --> 00:49:32.218
Now, please introduce yourselves.

652
00:49:34.096 --> 00:49:34.926
I'm Lee Seul-bi.

653
00:49:38.308 --> 00:49:39.598
My goodness.

654
00:49:39.976 --> 00:49:41.646
That's a beautiful name.

655
00:49:43.146 --> 00:49:43.976
It's a pleasure.

656
00:49:45.732 --> 00:49:47.572
How do you do?
I'm the new intern, Kim Hye-jin!

657
00:49:47.651 --> 00:49:49.611
I will put my heart and soul
into my work here!

658
00:49:51.405 --> 00:49:54.775
That's quite a voice you have there!

659
00:49:54.866 --> 00:49:57.236
This isn't the barracks,
so you can lower your voice.

660
00:49:57.369 --> 00:49:58.199
Yes, sir!

661
00:50:01.456 --> 00:50:04.246
Congratulations on joining the company.

662
00:50:04.918 --> 00:50:06.168
Thank you.

663
00:50:06.670 --> 00:50:09.130
Our job here at Management Support

664
00:50:09.214 --> 00:50:13.844
is to make sure that
the company runs smoothly.

665
00:50:14.052 --> 00:50:16.642
As the title infers,
we are a core division

666
00:50:16.930 --> 00:50:19.310
that both manages
and supports the company.

667
00:50:19.558 --> 00:50:21.058
Oh, that's right.

668
00:50:21.184 --> 00:50:22.024
Core division.

669
00:50:23.520 --> 00:50:27.150
I hope we can bring you both on board
as full-time employees in three months.

670
00:50:27.232 --> 00:50:28.152
I'll do my very best!

671
00:50:29.359 --> 00:50:30.989
My desk!

672
00:50:32.279 --> 00:50:34.659
Here are your intern ID badges.

673
00:50:34.865 --> 00:50:37.325
Ms. Lee, your picture came out well.

674
00:50:39.703 --> 00:50:41.413
-Please don't lose this.
-Thank you very much!

675
00:50:44.624 --> 00:50:45.884
{\an8}KIM HYE-JIN

676
00:50:47.627 --> 00:50:48.837
My ID badge!

677
00:50:50.130 --> 00:50:51.340
-Ms. Kim Hye-jin?
-Yes!

678
00:50:54.301 --> 00:50:55.591
Did you call for me, sir?

679
00:50:56.136 --> 00:50:57.466
That's why you're here, isn't it?

680
00:50:59.097 --> 00:51:02.557
This is the first assignment
I'm giving you.

681
00:51:02.642 --> 00:51:05.062
It's a very important job
that we are in charge of.

682
00:51:05.479 --> 00:51:07.059
Do you think you can handle it?

683
00:51:08.398 --> 00:51:09.648
You can depend on me on anything!

684
00:51:10.692 --> 00:51:13.152
<i>We have a reception every month</i>

685
00:51:13.236 --> 00:51:15.356
<i>for all the employees who have birthdays.</i>

686
00:51:15.447 --> 00:51:18.657
<i>We are in charge
of providing the refreshments.</i>

687
00:51:19.201 --> 00:51:21.581
<i>About 500 meters away
is a place called Woori Market.</i>

688
00:51:21.661 --> 00:51:23.001
<i>They've worked with us for many years,</i>

689
00:51:23.079 --> 00:51:25.749
<i>so that's where you'll go
for a ten percent discount.</i>

690
00:51:27.375 --> 00:51:28.625
Thank you very much!

691
00:51:29.669 --> 00:51:32.629
<i>Buy the gift cards for the event
at the post office.</i>

692
00:51:32.756 --> 00:51:35.926
<i>Oh, and can you pay my utility bill
while you're there?</i>

693
00:51:37.344 --> 00:51:40.064
<i>All campaigns are our responsibility too.</i>

694
00:51:40.722 --> 00:51:42.642
<i>I want you to put up
these posters on every floor.</i>

695
00:51:43.350 --> 00:51:46.140
<i>I trust that you won't use the elevator
while putting up</i>

696
00:51:46.228 --> 00:51:48.188
<i>these energy conservation posters.</i>

697
00:51:59.574 --> 00:52:01.164
I'm sorry.

698
00:52:04.329 --> 00:52:05.209
{\an8}I'm back!

699
00:52:07.332 --> 00:52:12.382
I didn't realize my job requires me
to run everywhere.

700
00:52:12.796 --> 00:52:15.416
You're completely out of breath!

701
00:52:15.799 --> 00:52:16.629
Are you all right?

702
00:52:17.467 --> 00:52:18.337
I'm fine!

703
00:52:19.219 --> 00:52:20.469
Then get me a cup of water.

704
00:52:20.637 --> 00:52:21.507
{\an8}Sorry?

705
00:52:21.721 --> 00:52:22.681
Water.

706
00:52:22.931 --> 00:52:23.771
Yes, sir.

707
00:52:30.689 --> 00:52:31.519
Nice!

708
00:52:33.441 --> 00:52:34.821
Can't you take that off at home?

709
00:52:35.235 --> 00:52:36.065
Why?

710
00:52:36.194 --> 00:52:38.244
I even take it to bed with me.

711
00:52:39.364 --> 00:52:40.204
That reminds me.

712
00:52:43.118 --> 00:52:45.658
Now that I'm getting a salary,
I'll pitch in from now on.

713
00:52:50.333 --> 00:52:51.173
Hey, Patriot.

714
00:52:52.168 --> 00:52:54.048
You've given me my independence.

715
00:52:54.838 --> 00:52:57.128
If it weren't for you,
my dad wouldn't have let me move out.

716
00:52:58.174 --> 00:53:00.434
So you hold onto this.

717
00:53:00.844 --> 00:53:03.184
Oh, please. I'm only a freeloader.

718
00:53:03.263 --> 00:53:04.853
-Take it.
-Forget it!

719
00:53:04.931 --> 00:53:06.471
-Take it.
-I said no!

720
00:53:06.558 --> 00:53:08.348
Take it!

721
00:53:15.400 --> 00:53:18.490
Mr. Boo, I've completed
the Excel spreadsheet and sent it to you.

722
00:53:19.404 --> 00:53:20.244
Already?

723
00:53:20.447 --> 00:53:24.327
Ms. Hye-jin, you're undoubtedly
the best worker here!

724
00:53:24.409 --> 00:53:27.579
That's why I endorsed your hiring!

725
00:53:28.830 --> 00:53:32.000
Are you the one who hired me?

726
00:53:32.292 --> 00:53:33.252
Didn't you know?

727
00:53:33.793 --> 00:53:37.553
I made it absolutely clear
that I wanted you

728
00:53:37.631 --> 00:53:39.421
as one of my new interns!

729
00:53:42.469 --> 00:53:46.179
<i>Female workers these days
always text men during work hours.</i>

730
00:53:46.264 --> 00:53:48.024
<i>They take hour-long breaks on the phone</i>

731
00:53:48.099 --> 00:53:49.559
<i>and refuse to work late</i>

732
00:53:49.643 --> 00:53:51.903
<i>because they want to go on dates.</i>

733
00:53:52.020 --> 00:53:55.070
<i>Some get married
within one year of being hired.</i>

734
00:53:55.649 --> 00:53:58.439
But what about our Ms. Kim?

735
00:53:58.860 --> 00:54:00.780
She's perfect!

736
00:54:00.862 --> 00:54:03.162
She doesn't receive any calls from men,

737
00:54:03.239 --> 00:54:05.909
and she has no dates to look forward to.

738
00:54:06.117 --> 00:54:06.947
I guess.

739
00:54:07.077 --> 00:54:08.577
A lacking résumé?

740
00:54:08.870 --> 00:54:10.620
That can be an advantage sometimes!

741
00:54:10.956 --> 00:54:12.746
She'll never be scouted
to another company.

742
00:54:16.211 --> 00:54:18.841
I'm a great judge of character!

743
00:54:18.922 --> 00:54:19.842
You're right!

744
00:54:23.176 --> 00:54:25.296
Mr. Boo, you're the best!

745
00:54:26.221 --> 00:54:27.721
Should I do something else?

746
00:54:28.139 --> 00:54:29.139
Do what?

747
00:54:29.224 --> 00:54:31.104
It's six o'clock, so get ready to go home.

748
00:54:32.477 --> 00:54:35.477
Take that box to <i>The Most</i> Editing Team.

749
00:54:35.814 --> 00:54:38.444
They always request things from us

750
00:54:38.525 --> 00:54:41.025
and never come to get it.

751
00:54:41.361 --> 00:54:42.651
<i>The Most</i> Editing Team?

752
00:54:56.960 --> 00:54:59.130
I didn't know we had this department.

753
00:55:05.093 --> 00:55:05.933
<i>Yes?</i>

754
00:55:06.136 --> 00:55:08.426
I'm here from
the Management Support Department.

755
00:55:15.937 --> 00:55:17.267
No way.

756
00:55:17.856 --> 00:55:19.436
-Come here!
-Okay!

757
00:55:20.692 --> 00:55:22.822
-Check this out and confirm. Hurry!
-Yes, ma'am.

758
00:55:38.668 --> 00:55:41.498
Please approve this layout.

759
00:55:47.719 --> 00:55:52.219
Wow, so this is the team
that creates the magazine.

760
00:56:00.940 --> 00:56:01.780
Excuse me.

761
00:56:02.275 --> 00:56:04.185
I'm from Management Support Department.

762
00:56:04.319 --> 00:56:05.529
The items that were requested...

763
00:56:05.612 --> 00:56:06.992
Just leave it anywhere there.

764
00:56:07.864 --> 00:56:08.744
In three minutes?

765
00:56:09.199 --> 00:56:10.699
-Yes.
-I'll put it here then.

766
00:56:11.034 --> 00:56:11.954
It's you.

767
00:56:14.162 --> 00:56:15.502
Go down and give this to a courier

768
00:56:16.456 --> 00:56:17.996
and come back for
the document translations.

769
00:56:18.083 --> 00:56:18.963
Sorry?

770
00:56:19.042 --> 00:56:22.132
It's door number 4444,
so don't ring all of the doors.

771
00:56:22.587 --> 00:56:24.007
And if you're going to work for me,

772
00:56:24.923 --> 00:56:27.263
you have to do something about that hair.

773
00:56:27.967 --> 00:56:30.177
This will pay for the courier.
I'm headed to the Art Department.

774
00:56:30.762 --> 00:56:33.772
Wait, why should I?

775
00:56:34.891 --> 00:56:36.231
Why am I doing this?

776
00:56:37.185 --> 00:56:39.395
I forgot to put these documents back.

777
00:56:42.565 --> 00:56:45.235
Are you here for <i>The Most</i> Editing Team?

778
00:56:45.652 --> 00:56:47.572
-Yes, I am.
-Here you go.

779
00:56:48.071 --> 00:56:48.911
Thank you!

780
00:56:53.993 --> 00:56:56.373
What was she saying?

781
00:56:57.705 --> 00:56:58.535
Wait...

782
00:56:59.958 --> 00:57:00.998
Where have I seen her before?

783
00:57:04.420 --> 00:57:05.340
You're back.

784
00:57:06.339 --> 00:57:07.219
Here.

785
00:57:08.466 --> 00:57:10.636
There are some typos.

786
00:57:11.010 --> 00:57:13.890
This was overlapped
with our 20th anniversary issue,

787
00:57:14.055 --> 00:57:16.305
so I barely have time
to write my own pieces.

788
00:57:17.600 --> 00:57:20.560
Also, look out for grammatical errors.

789
00:57:20.645 --> 00:57:22.105
I really need that done.

790
00:57:22.355 --> 00:57:23.185
What?

791
00:57:23.440 --> 00:57:24.770
What kind of editing?

792
00:57:25.358 --> 00:57:26.688
Excuse me.

793
00:57:26.860 --> 00:57:28.490
Why are you giving me this?

794
00:57:34.868 --> 00:57:36.408
Jun-u, who is she?

795
00:57:37.954 --> 00:57:38.874
That person?

796
00:57:39.080 --> 00:57:41.210
She's our new proofreading freelancer.

797
00:57:46.129 --> 00:57:50.129
There are only a few typos,
so it won't take you very long.

798
00:57:50.508 --> 00:57:51.338
What?

799
00:57:51.551 --> 00:57:53.931
I could swear that
we've met somewhere before.

800
00:57:54.095 --> 00:57:55.215
Have we?

801
00:57:55.555 --> 00:57:57.425
-No, we haven't.
-Did we meet at a club?

802
00:57:59.684 --> 00:58:02.104
I was wondering why I have to do this.

803
00:58:02.187 --> 00:58:03.437
Did you complete the translations?

804
00:58:03.521 --> 00:58:04.861
What? Oh, right.

805
00:58:05.648 --> 00:58:06.518
Here.

806
00:58:07.317 --> 00:58:08.227
Thank you.

807
00:58:09.611 --> 00:58:10.451
Yes.

808
00:58:12.572 --> 00:58:14.702
I'm curious. Why is everyone--

809
00:58:14.782 --> 00:58:17.492
Go to the café on the first floor
and take coffee to the studio

810
00:58:17.994 --> 00:58:19.754
at the building across from here.

811
00:58:20.747 --> 00:58:21.577
But...

812
00:58:44.562 --> 00:58:46.022
What's this place about?

813
00:58:52.153 --> 00:58:53.783
Now, we'll take ten!

814
00:58:54.280 --> 00:58:55.160
Coffee.

815
00:58:56.115 --> 00:58:57.025
Where is my coffee?

816
00:58:58.034 --> 00:58:59.834
The coffee is here!

817
00:59:03.456 --> 00:59:04.616
I'm so sorry.

818
00:59:05.959 --> 00:59:07.839
My apologies. I'm late, aren't I?

819
00:59:08.169 --> 00:59:09.879
There was a car accident on the way here.

820
00:59:10.171 --> 00:59:11.211
And you are?

821
00:59:11.673 --> 00:59:12.513
Sorry?

822
00:59:13.633 --> 00:59:16.143
I'm the new proofreading freelancer.

823
00:59:16.511 --> 00:59:17.391
What?

824
00:59:19.180 --> 00:59:20.560
<i>Then who's that girl with frizzy hair?</i>

825
00:59:21.015 --> 00:59:23.725
<i>She completed the translations
without any errors.</i>

826
00:59:24.143 --> 00:59:26.353
<i>I had her proofread my documents too.</i>

827
00:59:26.688 --> 00:59:27.688
<i>She did a great job.</i>

828
00:59:28.064 --> 00:59:29.364
<i>Who on earth is she?</i>

829
00:59:35.363 --> 00:59:36.243
Oh, no!

830
00:59:36.364 --> 00:59:38.124
Stop! Mister!

831
00:59:38.408 --> 00:59:39.408
MANAGEMENT SUPPORT DEPARTMENT

832
00:59:39.492 --> 00:59:41.412
<i>What?</i> The Most <i>Editing Team?</i>

833
00:59:42.078 --> 00:59:44.908
Why am I being reassigned there?

834
00:59:45.164 --> 00:59:47.714
They've requested your transfer.

835
00:59:47.875 --> 00:59:50.995
Ask them for the details
and return here after three months.

836
00:59:51.337 --> 00:59:53.457
What? For three months?

837
00:59:54.924 --> 00:59:57.054
But I'm prepared to do my best here
at Management Support.

838
00:59:57.135 --> 00:59:58.715
You can do that when you get back.

839
00:59:59.012 --> 01:00:00.392
Just go.

840
01:00:00.888 --> 01:00:03.348
<i>The Most</i> Editing Team
is the most influential department.

841
01:00:03.433 --> 01:00:04.813
We do whatever they demand.

842
01:00:05.059 --> 01:00:06.559
If you do a great job over there,

843
01:00:06.811 --> 01:00:08.861
it'll help you land
a full-time position here.

844
01:00:09.439 --> 01:00:10.269
But...

845
01:00:23.077 --> 01:00:24.577
Excuse me.

846
01:00:25.079 --> 01:00:26.579
Oh, you're here.

847
01:00:28.583 --> 01:00:29.963
Have a seat over there.

848
01:00:30.251 --> 01:00:31.751
-Over there?
-Yes.

849
01:00:32.003 --> 01:00:33.253
I look forward to working with you.

850
01:00:33.421 --> 01:00:34.261
Sure.

851
01:00:39.218 --> 01:00:40.258
She's here.

852
01:00:40.637 --> 01:00:42.177
I know I've seen her somewhere before.

853
01:00:42.722 --> 01:00:43.562
What?

854
01:00:49.937 --> 01:00:52.107
She looks awfully familiar.

855
01:00:54.609 --> 01:00:55.439
Yes, Ha-ri.

856
01:00:55.818 --> 01:00:57.028
What was your text about?

857
01:00:57.779 --> 01:00:58.819
Why were you transferred?

858
01:00:59.280 --> 01:01:00.410
I don't know.

859
01:01:00.865 --> 01:01:02.575
I don't know what's going on.

860
01:01:02.659 --> 01:01:03.619
<i>Buon giorno!</i>

861
01:01:04.118 --> 01:01:07.078
-Ma'am, you're here.
-How are you today?

862
01:01:08.122 --> 01:01:09.002
Ciao!

863
01:01:10.291 --> 01:01:12.001
The weather is wonderful outside!

864
01:01:12.418 --> 01:01:13.288
Goodness!

865
01:01:13.670 --> 01:01:16.340
An amazing lady just walked in.

866
01:01:16.964 --> 01:01:23.974
<i>Sometimes, without any warning,
your life takes an unexpected turn.</i>

867
01:01:24.347 --> 01:01:25.767
That's the guy from the elevator!

868
01:01:26.140 --> 01:01:27.640
Annoying jerk.

869
01:01:28.351 --> 01:01:32.231
Is he here yet?
I thought he was coming today.

870
01:01:33.022 --> 01:01:36.572
<i>That's why you must
always be on your toes.</i>

871
01:01:37.276 --> 01:01:38.566
Oh, there he is now.

872
01:01:38.986 --> 01:01:41.856
<i>Life isn't something you can prepare for.</i>

873
01:01:45.493 --> 01:01:46.333
Attention!

874
01:01:46.911 --> 01:01:48.081
Allow me to introduce him.

875
01:01:48.955 --> 01:01:53.915
He's the deputy chief editor transferred
from our New York head office.

876
01:01:55.420 --> 01:01:56.500
<i>Kim Hye-jin, are you there?</i>

877
01:01:57.380 --> 01:01:58.210
Hey!

878
01:01:58.923 --> 01:02:00.473
Oh, right!

879
01:02:01.384 --> 01:02:02.224
Michael Jackson!

880
01:02:02.552 --> 01:02:03.592
It's a pleasure to meet you.

881
01:02:03.845 --> 01:02:07.055
I'm your new deputy chief editor,
Ji Sung-joon.

882
01:02:07.390 --> 01:02:09.560
<i>None of us saw this coming.</i>

883
01:02:09.892 --> 01:02:11.642
<i>-This was the beginning...
-This was the beginning</i>

884
01:02:12.019 --> 01:02:14.269
<i>of our very own hidden picture puzzle.</i>

885
01:02:31.622 --> 01:02:32.672
Allow me to introduce him.

886
01:02:32.999 --> 01:02:33.919
I'm Ji Sung-joon.

887
01:02:34.375 --> 01:02:35.375
It's a pleasure to meet you.

888
01:02:35.501 --> 01:02:38.421
<i>Does this mean you'll have
to face Ji Sung-joon every day?</i>

889
01:02:38.755 --> 01:02:40.665
<i>Hey, what if he recognizes me?</i>

890
01:02:41.007 --> 01:02:42.837
<i>This is our very first team meeting.</i>

891
01:02:45.970 --> 01:02:46.970
Do you have a low IQ?

892
01:02:47.054 --> 01:02:49.724
I find it all offensive!

893
01:02:49.974 --> 01:02:52.144
<i>Didn't you say you wanted to work late
until your nose bleeds?</i>

894
01:02:52.310 --> 01:02:54.520
So why are you resigning
because of that Ji Sung-joon?

895
01:02:54.604 --> 01:02:55.774
I'm sorry.

896
01:02:56.439 --> 01:02:59.149
<i>Did you think you could hide this
from me forever?</i>

897
01:03:02.779 --> 01:03:04.779
Subtitle translation by: Hyelim Park

898
01:03:05.305 --> 01:04:05.757
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
